sis on fun something that  can be missing in the lives of young  carers given their circumstances scalped  works to provide help support and  information to carers of all ages  looking after a relative friend or  neighbor who thought through long-term  illness disability and other reasons may  need extra support to manage some  aspects of their daily lives and there  is a photograph accompanying this  article that shows I think a young  person kind of scrambling up a ladder  with a firefighter behind giving them a  friendly push if you'd like more  information on the SCAF you can visit  their website at WWDC fe org UK top  summer security tips to ensure you can  relax and enjoy the summer essex police  is crime prevention officer for the  rockford district Emma Clark has some  advice for keeping garden equipment safe  from theft top of her list of tips is  sheds and outbuildings security sheds  and outbuildings typically contain tools  and gardening equipment which are not  just valuable but could also prove  useful to a burglar looking to break  into your home secure the shed door with  pad bolts and closed shackle padlocks  that cannot be easily apprised off or  fit a padlock alarm hindi should be  fitted using culture bolts and large  backing washers doors can be further  secured with shed alarms and a shed bar  lock Emma said larger items such as  bikes ladders and lawn mowers should  ideally be chained to a shed shackle on  the wall or to an i-type anchor  fixed into a concrete floor inside the  shed it's advisable to make a note of  all gardening equipment recording the  make model and serial number and to mark  all items in a highly visible manner  such as scratching or inject engraving  or using a permanent Security marker  showing their postcode and house number  or name this will make them less  attractive to a thief if you keep your  gardening tools and equipment in your  garage don't advertise their presence to  passing strangers by leaving the door  ope